    <string name="guidance_title">Make sure calls always arrive</string>
    <string name="guidance_intro">Some phones stop apps that run in the background. Allow Two Way so calls still ring when the screen is off.</string>
    <string name="guidance_battery_button">Battery: allow background use</string>
    <string name="guidance_fullscreen_button">Allow calls on the lock screen</string>
    <string name="guidance_vendor_xiaomi">Xiaomi / Redmi / POCO: open Security, then Permissions, then Autostart and allow Two Way. In Battery saver choose No restrictions.</string>
    <string name="guidance_vendor_oppo">OPPO / Realme / OnePlus: open Settings, then Battery, then allow background activity and auto launch for Two Way.</string>
    <string name="guidance_vendor_vivo">vivo / iQOO: open iManager, then App manager, then Autostart and allow Two Way.</string>
    <string name="guidance_vendor_huawei">Huawei / Honor: open Settings, then Apps, then App launch, switch to Manage manually and enable all options for Two Way.</string>
    <string name="guidance_vendor_samsung">Samsung: open Settings, then Battery, then Background usage limits, and add Two Way to Never sleeping apps.</string>
    <string name="guidance_vendor_generic">If calls do not ring when the screen is off, look for battery optimisation or autostart settings for Two Way and allow them.</string>
